'''Agaminæ''' (ag-ạ-mī′nē), ''n. pl.'' [< ''Agama''<sup>1</sup> + ''-inæ''.] A subfamily of agamoid lizards with no wing-like lateral expansions, a mouth of moderate size, and small conical incisors. It embraces about 70 species, inhabiting Asia, Africa, and Australasia.

